#version 460
// UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-02 the REFERENCE path tracer ([Main.Main.RayTracing] ReferencePT; core\RtPathTrace.cpp; docs/next/RT-PATH-TRACING.md):
// a ground truth for the raster and hybrid look, not a real-time effect. Runs in the RT helper (NvrRtHelper.exe, 64-bit).
// Per pixel and frame PTSamples paths from the camera (sub-pixel jitter), each up to PTBounces bounces, diffuse (Lambert) everywhere:
//   - at every hit: its glow (the glow atlas, GlowTextures) x PTGlow is emitted; the sun (one ray inside the sun's disc, 0.53 deg) and
//     ONE of the given lamps (picked in proportion to its unshadowed light, a shadow ray) are sampled directly (next event estimation);
//   - the path goes on in a cosine-weighted direction (throughput x the hit's albedo: the albedo atlas with HitTextures, else the
//     record's average colour), Russian roulette from the third bounce;
//   - a ray that leaves the scene takes the sky's light: outdoors a gradient from the game's horizon to its sky colour (x PTSky), below
//     the horizon the horizon colour x 0.3; indoors PTAmbient x the game's ambient (default 0: interiors are lit by their lamps only).
// Units are the game's: a surface facing the sun gets albedo x the sun colour (no 1/pi), a sky of colour L all round gives albedo x L,
// so the result compares with the raster frame before its tonemap. (2026-11-07 ptaaa-materials: glass panes, light through leaves and grass,
// skin's scattering and cloth sheen, RT-PATH-TRACING.md section "ptaaa-materials"; still no particles.) What the RT scene holds
// (FORK-RT-CORE.md), lit by what this pass knows. (Normal maps: at traced hits through RtHit.glsl rtHitNormalMapped, the real maps with
// RealNormalMaps or the atlas with NormalTextures; specular with PTSpecular.)
// The running mean is kept in float32 (two RG32F images: fp16 stops moving after a few hundred samples); NVR resets it (p.accum.x = 0)
// when the camera, the sun or a setting moves, and copies the display image (RGBA16F, linear) back for RtPathTraceShow.frag.
// Compile: glslangValidator -V --target-env vulkan1.2 -o RtPathTrace.spv RtPathTrace.comp
// (2026-11-04) variant RtPathTraceGrid.spv: -DPT_LIGHT_GRID (PTLightGrid, Compute/variants.txt / compile-compute.sh): the lamps through a world
// grid. A variant, not a branch: with the grid code in the same shader its plain path cost ~6 % more (RT-PATH-TRACING.md section 25)
// (2026-11-04 d) variant RtPathTraceGI.spv: -DPT_RESTIR_GI (PTRestirGI with PTDenoise): the first bounce is a cosine sample written out
// for ReSTIR GI's reuse pass (RtRestirGI.comp), not added in here (section 29)
// (2026-11-07) PTRestirDI (flag 262144, not in the GI variant): the lamps at the first hit through ReSTIR DI, reservoirs kept in the
// helper's scratch store (binding 20, protocol 6) from frame to frame (section 47); PTRadianceCache (flag 524288): a world-space radiance
// cache in the same store gives the path's last hit the light of all further bounces (section 48; RtPathTraceCache.comp resolves it)
// (2026-11-07 ptaaa-emissive) PTEmissive (the frame row's texel 22 > 0, not in the GI variant): glowing TRIANGLES as lights, one sample a
// hit by their power (RtEmissiveBuild.comp's list, src/core/RtEmissiveRow.h), MIS against the bounce rays, in ReSTIR DI with the lamps
// (2026-11-07 ptaaa-denoiser) PTDenoiseSplit (flag 4194304, with PTDenoise's 512; not in the GI variant): the light written as two signals,
// diffuse (display) and specular (specOut, + the specular hit distance), each divided by its own albedo, for core\RtDenoise's split
// (RT-PATH-TRACING.md "ptaaa-denoiser"; the Path() hooks are marked ptaaa-denoiser)
// (2026-11-07 perf-ptcost, RT-PATH-TRACING.md section 67) the ray budget: ReSTIR DI's same-spot rule, one light sample at bounce hits, one
// camera query without the hidden body (LoadCostKeys; core\RtPtCost.h), and the RT host's ray count (gRayCount)
#extension GL_EXT_ray_query : require
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : enable

layout(local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8) in;

layout(set = 0, binding = 0) uniform accelerationStructureEXT scene;   // world minus CameraPosition, z up
layout(set = 0, binding = 1, std140) uniform Pass {   // core\RtPathTrace.cpp PassConstants
	vec4 size;          // w, h, 1 / w, 1 / h
	vec4 forward;       // the view's forward (scene axes), w farZ (the depth buffer's scale)
	vec4 right;         // right / P00
	vec4 up;            // up / P11
	vec4 origin;        // xyz the eye in scene space (RtCore::Eye), w the frame's random seed
	vec4 accum;         // x samples already in the mean (0: start over), y bounces, z paths a pixel this frame, w flags (1 alpha test,
	                    // 2 albedo atlas, 4 glow atlas, 8 the screen's G-buffer for the first hit, 16 the sky panorama,
	                    // 32 the frame, 64 the normal atlas, 128 PTSpecular, 256 the MaterialBuffer)
	vec4 sunDir;        // xyz toward the sun, w 1 = the sun lights (outdoors, above the horizon)
	vec4 sunColor;      // rgb linear, w the sun disc's half-angle tangent
	vec4 skyZenith;     // rgb linear x PTSky, w 1 = outdoors (the sky on misses)
	vec4 skyHorizon;    // rgb linear x PTSky, w PTGlow
	vec4 ambient;       // rgb the interior's light on misses (the game's ambient x PTAmbient), w PTSky (the panorama's scale, flag 16)
	vec4 misc;          // x lamps given (0-8), y PTClamp (a path's luminance cap, 0 none), z ray length, w DebugView (0 the picture, 1 albedo,
	                    // 2 normals, 3 the first hit's direct light only, 4 roughness red / metal green, 5 (2026-11-03) the first hit's
                    // arriving indirect light in RT GI's bounce units: hit albedo x its light, no first albedo, no first direct),
                    // (2026-11-03 rtspec) 8 the first hit's DIRECT highlight only (sun + lamps + glow lights, the GGX lobe, no diffuse),
                    // 9 the first hit's REFLECTION only (what its GGX lobe sees from one bounce on: the lit room, glow, sky; no direct)
	vec4 lampPos[8];    // xyz scene space, w reach
	vec4 lampColor[8];  // rgb linear x dimmer
	vec4 rect;          // (2026-11-03) xy the depth's jitter (screen uv: TAA / FSR / DLSS; the G-buffer pixel lies on the unjittered ray
	                    // through uv + this), z glow lights in the lamp image after the lamps (PTGlowLights, with flag 1024), w unused. size = the RenderScale rect at RenderScale < 1 (the G-buffer's top-left part)
	vec4 grid[3];       // (2026-11-04) PTLightGrid (RtPathTraceGrid.spv only): [0] xyz the grid's low corner (scene space), w cells x; [1] xyz
	                    // 1 / the cell size, w cells y; [2] x cells z, y the grid rows' width (texels); (b) [2].z PTBounceDistance, [2].w PTIndirectClamp
} p;                    // (the block is full: 512 bytes. (2026-11-04 b) rect.w = PTBounceAlpha)
layout(set = 0, binding = 2, rg32f) uniform image2D accumA;        // the running mean's red, green
layout(set = 0, binding = 3, rg32f) uniform image2D accumB;        // its blue, the samples
layout(set = 0, binding = 4, rgba16f) uniform writeonly image2D display;
layout(set = 0, binding = 5, r16f) uniform readonly image2D alphaAtlas;     // the core's (or a stand-in, flag 1 off)
layout(set = 0, binding = 6, rgba8) uniform readonly image2D albedoAtlas;   // (or a stand-in, flag 2 off)
layout(set = 0, binding = 7, rgba8) uniform readonly image2D glowAtlas;     // (or a stand-in, flag 4 off)
// (2026-11-02 b) PTPrimary: the screen's G-buffer for the first hit (flag 8): TESR_DepthBuffer (view z / farZ), TESR_NormalsBuffer (view
// space x 0.5 + 0.5: the interpolated vertex normals, no normal maps), TESR_AlbedoBuffer (linear base colour, a 1 where written);
// the sky panorama (flag 16, RT reflections' SkyPanorama: 128 x 128 hemi-octahedral, linear, the sky as the screen saw it)
layout(set = 0, binding = 8, r32f) uniform readonly image2D gDepth;
layout(set = 0, binding = 9, rgba16f) uniform readonly image2D gNormals;
layout(set = 0, binding = 12, rgba16f) uniform readonly image2D gAlbedo;      // (pass image 8: the helper's extra bindings start at 12)
layout(set = 0, binding = 13, rgba16f) uniform readonly image2D skyPano;      // (pass image 9)
// (2026-11-02 c) the game's frame as drawn at the RT core's point (flag 32; the stored curve: x^2.2 = linear): what a camera ray that
// leaves the RT scene sees (the sky with its clouds exactly, the far land and LOD the scene lacks)
layout(set = 0, binding = 14, rgba16f) uniform readonly image2D gFrame;      // (pass image 10)
layout(set = 0, binding = 15, rgba8) uniform readonly image2D normalAtlas;    // (pass image 11; 2026-11-02 d: NormalTextures, flag 64)
layout(set = 0, binding = 16, rgba16f) uniform readonly image2D gMaterial;    // (pass image 12; 2026-11-02 e: TESR_MaterialBuffer, flag 256)
// (2026-11-03) PTDenoise's albedo demodulation (flag 512): the display gets the light / the first surface's colour (what the denoiser
// smooths: no texture to blur), this image the colour itself (RtPathTraceShow.frag multiplies it back after the denoiser)
layout(set = 0, binding = 17, rgba16f) uniform writeonly image2D albedoOut;  // (pass image 13)
// (2026-11-03) all the frame's lamps (flag 1024; misc.x = how many, up to 80): lamp k at texels 4k..4k+3 = pos.xy, pos.z + reach,
// colour.rg, colour.b + 0 (RG32F; scene space, linear x dimmer)
// (2026-11-03 b) PTGlowLights: after the lamps, rect.z glow lights (glow-mapped instances' world bound spheres): centre.xy, centre.z +
// radius, a guess of their light (rg, b + 0: only steers which light is picked, never what it gives)
// (2026-11-04) PTLightGrid (RtPathTraceGrid.spv): rows 1.. of the same image, read as one run of texels t (x t % width, y 1 + t / width):
// per cell (z x cells y + y) x cells x + x one texel (its list's first entry, how many), then the lists, two lamp numbers a texel (entry
// e at float 2 x cells + e). Each cell lists, in rising order, every lamp whose reach meets it (core\RtPathTrace.cpp BuildGrid)
layout(set = 0, binding = 18, rg32f) uniform readonly image2D lampImage;     // (pass image 14)
#ifndef PT_RESTIR_GI
// UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-07 the helper's scratch store (protocol 6, NVR_RT_BINDING_SCRATCH): zero at the helper's start, kept between frames.
// Words [0, 12 w h): the ReSTIR DI reservoirs, two sets of w x h (the traced rect's size) x 6 words (since ptaaa-emissive; StoreReservoir
// has the layout), this frame writing set FrameParity(). From the frame row's cache base on: the radiance cache (section 48), then
// PTEmissive's blocks + list (LoadScratchLayout checks the regions: ptaaa-hangfix).
layout(set = 0, binding = 20, std430) buffer Scratch { uint words[]; } scratch;
// UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-07 (ptaaa-denoiser) PTDenoiseSplit (flag 4194304, with 512): the specular signal apart from the diffuse one (NRD
// ReLAX's split). display = the diffuse light / the first surface's colour (as before: albedoOut), this image = (the specular light /
// its specular albedo, the first bounce ray's hit distance when that ray was the specular lobe's: 60000 a miss, 0 unknown); the mean
// images (unused under PTDenoise) carry the specular albedo the light was divided by: accumA = (r, g), accumB = (b, roughness).
// (pass image 15; the GI variant has its own image there and no split)
layout(set = 0, binding = 19, rgba16f) uniform writeonly image2D specOut;
#endif
// (2026-11-07) the lamp image's FRAME ROW (row 1 + kGridRows = 49; core\RtPathTrace.cpp FrameRow): per-frame values the full constant
// block has no room for, two floats a texel: 0-1 last frame's forward (xyz, w 1 = its reservoirs are valid), 2-3 right, 4-5 up (as the
// pass's: / P00, / P11), 6-7 last frame's eye in this frame's scene space + this frame's reservoir set (0 / 1), 8-9 the camera's world
// position (the scene's origin in the world: the cache's cells are world cells) + log2 of the cache's entries, 10 PTRestirMaxM,
// PTRestirDISpatial (neighbours), 11 their radius (pixels), the normal test (cos), 12 the plane test (share of the distance), the
// cache's first word / 4096; (2026-11-07 ptaaa-emissive) 22 PTEmissive's instances, their scratch words' start / 4096. Row 50 after it:
// PTEmissive's instances (src/core/RtEmissiveRow.h)
const int kFrameRow = 49;
vec2 FrameTexel(int i) { return imageLoad(lampImage, ivec2(i, kFrameRow)).rg; }
#ifdef PT_RESTIR_GI
// (2026-11-04 d) PTRestirGI: the path's light WITHOUT what came through the first bounce (the first hit's glow and direct light, or the
// whole path where there is no first surface), for RtRestirGI.comp. The first-bounce sample itself goes into the mean images (unused
// with PTDenoise): accumA = (its direction packed, the hit distance; 0 = the sky), accumB = (the hit's normal packed, the first hit's
// normal packed with its glossy share), display = (the light arriving along it, the first hit's distance along the camera ray; 0 = no
// surface); albedoOut.a = 1 + the first surface's metal (RtPathTraceShow.frag clamps it to 1)
layout(set = 0, binding = 19, rgba16f) uniform writeonly image2D giDirect;   // (pass image 15)
#include "RtRestirGI.glsl"
#endif
#define RT_ALPHA_ATLAS alphaAtlas
#define RT_ALBEDO_ATLAS albedoAtlas
#define RT_GLOW_ATLAS glowAtlas
#define RT_NORMAL_ATLAS normalAtlas
// UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-07 (ptaaa-materials) glass panes (record kind 1) are passed by every other shader's alpha test; here a ray meets them
// when this is true (Path sets it per ray: bounce rays always, the camera's with PTGlass 2). Shadow rays never stop at them (Visible tints).
bool gGlassSolid = false;
#define RT_ALPHA_GLASS_SOLID gGlassSolid
float gHairKind = 0.0;   // (2026-11-10) frame row texel 30.x bit 2 (BlendedHair): hair's own highlight, and its alpha as a blend's coverage
#define RT_ALPHA_BLEND_TINTED (gHairKind > 0.5)   // (hair is blended by the game: its alpha blocks that share of the rays, RtAlpha.glsl; off with BlendedHair false: the plain cut as before)
#include "RtAlpha.glsl"
#include "RtHit.glsl"
#include "RtHidden.glsl"   // (2026-11-07 ptaaa-firstperson) rays near the eye pass over the hidden first-person body

// ---- UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-07 (ptaaa-hangfix) GPU hang guards: the merged path tracer lost the AMD iGPU (Windows event 4101, a TDR) now and then.
// None of these changes a result where the data is sane; each keeps a broken input (a NaN, a bad count, a stale or overlapping scratch
// header) from running a wave for ever or reading / writing past a buffer (the helper has no robustBufferAccess: on AMD an out-of-range
// storage buffer access can fault the GPU). RT-PATH-TRACING.md "ptaaa-hangfix".
//  - every ray query starts through PT_RAY_INIT: a ray whose origin or direction is not finite, whose direction is zero, or whose
//    [tMin, tMax] is not a finite range from 0 up (undefined behaviour in Vulkan; a NaN ray can keep AMD's traversal looping) becomes an
//    empty ray (the eye, up, [0, 0]) that meets nothing;
//  - every rayQueryProceedEXT loop ends after kPtMaxCandidates candidates (rayQueryTerminateEXT: what was confirmed so far stands); a ray
//    through the densest test scenes meets a few dozen cut-out / glass candidates.
const uint kPtMaxCandidates = 256u;
const int kPtMaxLamps = 256, kPtMaxLights = 288;   // the lamp image: RtPathTrace.cpp kLampsMax lamps + kGlowMax glow lights
const int kPtMaxBounces = 64, kPtMaxPaths = 64;   // (PTBounces / PTSamples go to 16; the RT host's furnaces trace 48 bounces)
bool PtRayOk(vec3 o, vec3 d, float tMin, float tMax) {
	// (one sum: a NaN or Inf anywhere in it fails the first test; sane values are far below 1e30)
	const float s = abs(o.x) + abs(o.y) + abs(o.z) + abs(d.x) + abs(d.y) + abs(d.z) + tMax;
	return s < 1.0e30 && dot(d, d) > 1.0e-12 && tMax >= tMin && tMin >= 0.0;
}
uint gRayCount = 0u;   // (perf-ptcost) this thread's ray queries (the RT host's count mode: LoadCostKeys)
#ifndef PT_PICK_FLOOR
#define PT_PICK_FLOOR 0.1   // (perf-ptcost) PTBounceLights 0's floor (Direct); the RT host's ptcost scene: 0.25 +6 % noise, 0.1 +3 %, 0.02 +1 %
#endif
#define PT_RAY_INIT(Q, FLAGS, MASK, O, TMIN, D, TMAX) { vec3 o_ = (O), d_ = (D); float t0_ = (TMIN), t1_ = (TMAX); gRayCount++; \
	if (!PtRayOk(o_, d_, t0_, t1_)) { o_ = vec3(0.0); d_ = vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0); t0_ = 0.0; t1_ = 0.0; } \
	rayQueryInitializeEXT(Q, scene, FLAGS, MASK, o_, t0_, d_, t1_); }
// at the top of a rayQueryProceedEXT loop's body (N: a uint 0 declared before the loop)
#define PT_GUARD(Q, N) if (++N > kPtMaxCandidates) { rayQueryTerminateEXT(Q); break; }
#define PT_PROCEED_OPAQUE(Q) { uint n_ = 0u; while (rayQueryProceedEXT(Q)) { PT_GUARD(Q, n_) } }
// a count from a constant or the lamp image, NaN-safe, in [0, hi]
int PtCount(float x, int hi) { return x > 0.0 ? min(int(min(x, float(hi)) + 0.5), hi) : 0; }

bool AlphaTest() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 1u) != 0u; }
bool AlbedoAtlas() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 2u) != 0u; }
bool GlowAtlas() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 4u) != 0u; }
bool GBuffer() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 8u) != 0u; }
bool SkyPanorama() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 16u) != 0u; }
bool ScreenFrame() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 32u) != 0u; }
bool NormalAtlas() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 64u) != 0u; }
bool LampImage() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 1024u) != 0u; }
// (2026-11-05) PTGlowFromFrame (flag 8192): a glowing surface the camera sees where the game's frame shows it takes the frame's pixel
bool GlowFromFrame() { return (uint(p.accum.w) & 8192u) != 0u; }
// (2026-11-03 rtspec) PTGameLamps (flag 2048): a lamp falls off as the game lights it (Pointlights.hlsl vanillaAtt 1 - (d/r)^2, decoded
// like a colour by LinFalloff: FalloffMatch 1, gamma 2.2; LampFalloff's shape off, the default); else (1 - d/r)^2, as RT GI
// (2026-11-06 c) PTLampFalloff 1 (flag 131072): physical, windowed inverse square. The reach is the game's x 2 here (RtPathTrace.cpp), so x =
// d / (2 r) and the game's own x is 2x: K / ((2x)^2 + e^2) x (1 - x^4)^2, e = 0.2 of the game radius (a lamp's size: no spike at it),
// K = 0.0612 = the same total light over the sphere as (1 - x^2)^2.2 out to r (RT-PATH-TRACING section 45). No rim: it fades to 0 at 2 r.
float LampFall(float x) {
	if ((uint(p.accum.w) & 131072u) != 0u) { const float w = max(1.0 - x * x * x * x, 0.0); return 0.0612 / (4.0 * x * x + 0.04) * w * w; }
	return (uint(p.accum.w) & 2048u) != 0u ? pow(max(1.0 - x * x, 0.0), 2.2) : (1.0 - x) * (1.0 - x);
}
bool gBackSide = false;   // (2026-11-07 ptaaa-materials) Translucent: the light from behind a thin leaf / ear (no glow light sample there)
int GlowLightCount() { return LampImage() && !gBackSide ? PtCount(p.rect.z, kPtMaxLights - kPtMaxLamps) : 0; }   // (hangfix: capped)
int LampCount() { return PtCount(p.misc.x, kPtMaxLamps); }   // (hangfix: misc.x, capped at the lamp image's lamps)
#ifdef PT_LIGHT_GRID
vec2 GridTexel(int t) { const int width = max(int(p.grid[2].y + 0.5), 1); return   // (hangfix: no % 0)
	 imageLoad(lampImage, ivec2(t % width, 1 + t / width)).rg; }
#endif

// UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-07 (rtgap-tess; docs/next/RT-DETAIL-GAPS.md section 1, RT-PATH-TRACING.md section 56) the frame row's texels 16-21
// (core/RtTessContact.h PackRow; with the lamp image, flag 1024): 16-17 the bumps' slack (Strength, FadeStart, FadeEnd), 18-19 PTContactShadows
// (pixels, longest, thickness, strength), 20-21 its gate. (1a) a screen surface up to the slack off the traced flat one is the same surface;
// (1b) the first hit's sun and lamp rays also take the depth buffer's contact march (Direct, RestirLamps).
#define RT_CONTACT_DEPTH gDepth
#include "RtContact.glsl"
vec4 PtSlack() { return LampImage() ? vec4(FrameTexel(16), FrameTexel(17)) : vec4(0.0); }
bool gContact = false;   // set at the first hit while the screen's surface is known (Path): its point, normal, view depth
vec3 gContactFrom = vec3(0.0), gContactN = vec3(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
float gContactZ = 0.0, gContactNoise = 0.0;
float PtContact(vec3 toLight, float lightDist) {
	if (!gContact) return 1.0;
	return rtContactShadow(gContactFrom, gContactN, toLight, lightDist, gContactZ, p.forward, p.right.xyz, p.up.xyz, vec3(0.0), p.rect.xy, p.size.xy,
		vec4(FrameTexel(18), FrameTexel(19)), vec4(FrameTexel(20), FrameTexel(21)), gContactNoise);
}

// PCG (O'Neill 2014) per pixel, frame, path and dimension: no pattern between pixels, independent frames
uint state;
uint Pcg() { state = state * 747796405u + 2891336453u; uint w = ((state >> ((state >> 28u) + 4u)) ^ state) * 277803737u; return (w >> 22u) ^ w; }
float Rand() { return float(Pcg() >> 8) * (1.0 / 16777216.0); }

// A rayQueryEXT cannot be a parameter: alpha-tested candidates (mask 0x10) are confirmed only where their texture is solid
// (ptaaa-hangfix) both with the candidate cap (PT_GUARD)
// (2026-11-11 hair-through) the nearest hair card (a tinted record, flags 0x60) the current ray's alpha test let it pass, as a distance
// along the ray; 1e30 = none. Reset before each ray of the path, read for the camera's ray only (the first-hit choice in Trace).
float gHairSkipT = 1.0e30;
#define PT_NOTE_HAIR_SKIP(q) { if ((records[rayQueryGetIntersectionInstanceIdEXT(q, false)].flags & 0x60u) == 0x60u) \
	gHairSkipT = min(gHairSkipT, rayQueryGetIntersectionTEXT(q, false)); }
#define Proceed(q) { uint n_ = 0u; while (rayQueryProceedEXT(q)) { PT_GUARD(q, n_) \
	if (rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, false) == gl_RayQueryCandidateIntersectionTriangleEXT) { \
	if (rtAlphaPass(rayQueryGetIntersectionInstanceIdEXT(q, false), uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionPrimitiveIndexEXT(q, false)), \
		rayQueryGetIntersectionBarycentricsEXT(q, false))) rayQueryConfirmIntersectionEXT(q); else PT_NOTE_HAIR_SKIP(q) } } }
// (2026-11-07 rtgap-decals) shadow / visibility rays: decals (NVR_RT_CUSTOM_DECAL) never block them (RtAlpha.glsl rtAlphaPassShadow). (With
// AlphaTest() off there are no decals in the scene: the core takes them only with its alpha atlas.)
#define ProceedShadow(q) { uint n_ = 0u; while (rayQueryProceedEXT(q)) { PT_GUARD(q, n_) \
	if (rayQueryGetIntersectionTypeEXT(q, false) == gl_RayQueryCandidateIntersectionTriangleEXT && \
	rtAlphaPassShadow(rayQueryGetIntersectionInstanceCustomIndexEXT(q, false), rayQueryGetIntersectionInstanceIdEXT(q, false), \
		uint(rayQueryGetIntersectionPrimitiveIndexEXT(q, false)), rayQueryGetIntersectionBarycentricsEXT(q, false))) rayQueryConfirmIntersectionEXT(q); } }

// ---- UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-07 (ptaaa-materials, RT-PATH-TRACING.md section "materials") the material models' keys: the lamp image's frame row
// texels 24-26 (core\RtMaterials.h; with the lamp image, flag 1024): x PTGlass (0 off, 1 the light, 2 the camera too), y PTGlassTint,
// z PTFoliage, w PTSkin; texel 26 x PTClothSheen. Without the lamp image: all off.
// (merge 2026-11-07, the size fix) read once per thread (LoadMatKeys at main's start), not at each of ~100 inlined uses
vec4 gMatKeys = vec4(0.0);
float gMatSheen = 0.0;
float gMirrorSurface = 0.0;   // (2026-11-09 pt-mirrors) frame row texel 26.y (RtMaterials.h mirrorSurface)
void LoadMatKeys() {
	const bool on = (uint(p.accum.w) & 1024u) != 0u;
	gMatKeys = on ? vec4(FrameTexel(24), FrameTexel(25)) : vec4(0.0);
	gMatSheen = on ? FrameTexel(26).x : 0.0;
	gMirrorSurface = on ? FrameTexel(26).y : 0.0;   // (2026-11-09 pt-mirrors) PTDenoiseMirrorSurface: the roughness under which it applies (0 off)
}
vec4 MatKeys() { return gMatKeys; }
// ---- UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-09 PTBounceRoughen (the frame row's texel 27.x; core\RtPathTrace.cpp): path regularisation. A path that has
// left a matte (or rough) surface and then meets a smooth one finds a lamp or a glow through a needle-thin lobe: rare and hundreds of
// times brighter than its neighbours, one white pixel for a frame (a tester's screenshot: dots over the floor round a chrome and a gold
// ball; gone with PTSpecular off). No denoiser removes those reliably, and DLSS Ray Reconstruction is handed them raw. With the key on,
// a surface met AFTER a bounce is at least (the roughest bounce so far x the key) rough: the light a matte floor gets by way of a chrome
// ball is spread over a wider lobe (the same energy, far less variance; such "caustic" light comes out softer), while what the CAMERA
// sees in a mirror, and a mirror seen in a mirror, stay as sharp as before (their paths' bounces so far were smooth). 0 = off.
// UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-10 PTCacheShort (frame row texel 27.y; 0 = off): the radiance cache as a SHORTCUT (as NVIDIA's SHaRC uses its cache), not
// only as the last hit's top-up. Measured (tools/nvr-rt-playground, the room, 320 x 180 on the iGPU): PTRealtime's trace 63 ms, of which the
// cache 25 ms, while the cache never made a path shorter. With the key at N, one path in N is traced in full as before (those keep the cache
// fed at every depth); the others END at their first bounce hit when the cache has a settled cell there: that hit's own direct light is
// traced as before, and everything further comes from the cell (the same value a full path's last hit takes). A hit without a settled
// cell goes on in full. Cost: the light of the second bounce on is as coarse as the cache's cells (PTCacheCell) everywhere, not only at
// the path's end.
float gBounceRoughen = 0.0, gCacheShort = 0.0;
void LoadBounceRoughen() { const vec2 k = LampImage() ? FrameTexel(27) : vec2(0.0); gBounceRoughen = clamp(k.x, 0.0, 1.0); gCacheShort = clamp(k.y, 0.0, 64.0); }
float MatSheen() { return gMatSheen; }
// ---- UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-07 (perf-ptcost, RT-PATH-TRACING.md section "perf-ptcost") the ray budget's keys: the frame row's texels 28-29
// (core\RtPtCost.h PackRow; with the lamp image, flag 1024; without it all 0). 0 is the cheap path everywhere:
//   28.x PTRestirDIRays: 0 ReSTIR DI's targets hold visibility as before, but last frame's reservoir at the SAME SPOT (its point within
//        1.5 pixels: a still camera) needs no rays (its sample was seen there); 1 every ray as before (canonical 1-2, temporal 2, 2 per
//        spatial neighbour); test values: 2 unshadowed targets + one final ray (RTXDI's final visibility, W 0 when occluded), 3 as 0 +
//        one shadow ray for the canonical candidates' winner + the neighbours' MIS weights unshadowed (no rays at the neighbours). (With
//        PTRestirDISpatial 2, the new default: host scene restirdi 2.0 ReSTIR rays a pixel vs 3.3, the same mean and noise.)
//   28.y PTBounceLights: 0 a bounce hit (and a thin leaf's far side) takes ONE light sample, the sun, the picked lamp or the emissive point,
//        chosen in proportion to their unshadowed light (one shadow ray); 1 all three, a shadow ray each (before)
//   29.x 1: no instance of this frame is the hidden first-person body (NVR_RT_CUSTOM_HIDDEN): the camera ray is ONE query over everything
//        (0x7F), not the world's then the cut-outs' and people's (two)
//   29.y 1 (the RT host's NVR_RT_HOST_PTCOST count mode only): the display's alpha = 1 + this pixel's ray queries this frame (gRayCount)
float gRestirRays = 0.0, gBounceLights = 0.0, gOneCameraQuery = 0.0;
bool gCountRays = false;
// UNOFFICIAL 2026-11-10 (the frame row's texel 30; measured on an NVIDIA L4 by replaying a captured Lucky 38 frame, tools/nvr-rt-helper
// rt_capcheck + the cloud jobs: of the pass's 4.96 ms the first surface is 0.34, its direct light 0.73, the three bounces 1.44 + 1.52 +
// 0.93; with the lamp list off the whole pass is 2.11):
//   30.x unused (TRIED and removed the same day: picking the bounce hits' lamp from 1 / 2 / 4 lamps of the cell's list instead of all of
//        them: 4.95-4.99 ms against 4.96, no gain; the lamps' cost is their shadow rays, not the list)
//   30.y PTRouletteFrom 1: Russian roulette from the first bounce on (0: from the third, as before). A path is kept in proportion to
//        what it still carries, at least 1 in 4 here (its light x at most 4: under PTRealtimeClamp), so most second and third bounces off
//        this game's dark surfaces are never traced.
//   30.x BlendedHair (2026-11-10): 1 = a camera ray that meets HAIR (a tinted cut-out record) nearer than the screen's surface keeps the
//        traced hair as its first surface. The game's blend-only hair writes no depth, colour or normal into the G-buffer: the screen
